Here’s the complete HTML you can paste into your web page. It creates a new Google Maps view centered on the library, adds a “State Library” marker, and overlays three circles at the requested coordinates.

```html
<!-- Google Maps embed (static map) -->
<div style="width:600px;height:400px;">
  <iframe
    width="600"
    height="400"
    frameborder="0"
    style="border:0"
    src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed/v1/view?key=YOUR_API_KEY
         &center=34.052235,-118.243683
         &zoom=15
         &maptype=roadmap"
    allowfullscreen>
  </iframe>
</div>

<!-- Script to add the marker and circles (requires the JavaScript Maps API) -->
<script src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=YOUR_API_KEY"></script>
<script>
  function initMap() {
    const map = new google.maps.Map(document.querySelector('iframe').contentWindow.document.body, {
      center: { lat: 34.052235, lng: -118.243683 },
      zoom: 15,
      mapTypeId: 'roadmap'
    });

    // State Library marker
    new google.maps.Marker({
      position: { lat: 34.052235, lng: -118.243683 },
      map,
      title: 'State Library'
    });

    // Circle style (you can adjust color/opacity as needed)
    const circleOptions = {
      map,
      radius: 30,               // radius in metres – change as you wish
      fillColor: '#4285F4',
      fillOpacity: 0.35,
      strokeColor: '#4285F4',
      strokeOpacity: 0.8,
      strokeWeight: 2
    };

    // 1️⃣ Circle at 34.052235, -118.243683
    new google.maps.Circle({
      ...circleOptions,
      center: { lat: 34.052235, lng: -118.243683 }
    });

    // 2️⃣ Circle at 34.053690, -118.2423732
    new google.maps.Circle({
      ...circleOptions,
      center: { lat: 34.053690, lng: -118.2423732 }
    });

    // 3️⃣ Circle at 34.05381, -118.242751
    new google.maps.Circle({
      ...circleOptions,
      center: { lat: 34.05381, lng: -118.242751 }
    });
  }

  // Load the map once the page is ready
  window.addEventListener('load', initMap);
</script>
```

### What the code does
| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| **Embed** | Shows a 600 × 400 px map centered on the library (latitude 34.052235, longitude ‑118.243683) with zoom 15. |
| **Marker** | Places a marker titled **“State Library”** at the same coordinates. |
| **Circles** | Draws three circles (30 m radius by default) at the three coordinate pairs you supplied. You can change the `radius` value or the visual styling (`fillColor`, `strokeColor`, etc.) to suit your design. |

> **Important:** Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with a valid Google Maps JavaScript API key that has the *Maps Embed* and *Maps JavaScript* services enabled. If you only need a static image, you can keep the `<iframe>` alone and drop the JavaScript portion.  

Now just copy the snippet into the HTML of your page, supply your API key, and the map with the marker and circles will appear. Enjoy!

