| Situation | Recommended URL pattern | Why it works |
|-----------|--------------------------|--------------|
| **Simple static site** (e.g., GitHub Pages) | `https://yourdomain.com/soundcloud-callback.html` | You can embed a tiny JavaScript snippet that reads the query string (`?code=…`) and forwards it to your backend via AJAX. |
| **Server‑side app** (Node, PHP, Python, etc.) | `https://yourdomain.com/auth/soundcloud/callback` | A dedicated route that your server can process, store the token in a session or DB, then redirect the user to the final page (e.g., dashboard). |
| **Local development** | `http://localhost:3000/auth/soundcloud/callback` | Most OAuth providers (including SoundCloud) allow `http://localhost` URLs for testing. Just add it to the app settings. |
| **Multiple environments** (dev, staging, prod) | Register **each** URL separately in the SoundCloud app console (e.g., `https://dev.example.com/...`, `https://staging.example.com/...`, `https://example.com/...`). | SoundCloud validates the exact string, so you need a match for every environment you’ll use. |

**Key rules:**
- Must be a **fully qualified URL** (including `http://` or `https://`).  
- Must **exactly match** one of the URLs you entered in the SoundCloud developer console.  
