Below is a **step‑by‑step recipe** you can copy‑paste into any web page to give your form fields a “live‑typing” feel.  
The core of the effect is the **SVG typing animation** that the `createTypingSVG` function generates.  
Everything else is just ordinary HTML + JavaScript that swaps the SVG into a `<label>` (or a `<span>` next to the input) when the user focuses the field.

---

## 1️⃣  What the animation does

| Moment | What the user sees |
|--------|--------------------|
| **Page load** | A static placeholder (e.g., “Your name”) is shown. |
| **Focus** | After a short delay the SVG starts “typing” the placeholder text, character by character. |
| **Blur (optional)** | The text can be erased (deletion animation) and the static placeholder returns, or you can leave the typed text in place. |

All timing (delay, typing speed, deletion speed, pause before re‑type) is fully configurable via the helper functions:

* `setTypingAnimation({delayBeforeStart, typingSpeed})`
* `customizeDeletionAnimation({deletionSpeed, pauseBeforeRetyping})`

---

## 2️⃣  Minimal HTML skeleton

```html
