<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Form with typing animation</title>
  <style>
    .form‑field {
      position: relative;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .typing‑placeholder {
      position: absolute;
      left: 0.75rem;
      top: 50%;
      transform: translateY(-50%);
      pointer‑events: none;               /* lets clicks go to the input */
      color: #777;
      font-family: sans-serif;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
    input {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<form id="demo‑form">
  <div class="form‑field">
    <input type="text" id="name" autocomplete="off">
    <span class="typing‑placeholder" data‑svg‑id=""></span>
  </div>

  <div class="form‑field">
    <input type="email" id="email" autocomplete="off">
    <span class="typing‑placeholder" data‑svg‑id=""></span>
  </div>

  <button type="submit">Submit</button>
</form>

<script src="typing‑animation‑api.js"></script>   <!-- ← the JS that exposes the functions -->
<script>
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 2️⃣  Helper: create a typing‑SVG for a given placeholder text
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  async function makePlaceholderSVG(text, opts = {}) {
    const {fontColor = '#777', fontFamily = 'sans-serif', fontSize = 14, typingSpeed = 80} = opts;
    const svg = await createTypingSVG({
      text,
      fontColor,
      fontFamily,
      fontSize,
      typingSpeed
    });
    // The function returns an object like {svgId, svgMarkup}
    // We only need the markup to inject into the DOM.
    return svg.svgMarkup;
  }

  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  // 3️⃣  Initialise each field with its own SVG placeholder
  // -----------------------------------------------------------------
  const fields = [
    {input: document.getElementById('name'), placeholder: 'Enter your name…'},
    {input: document.getElementById('email'), placeholder: 'Enter your e‑mail…'}
  ];

  fields.forEach(async ({input, placeholder}) => {
    const span = input.parentElement.querySelector('.typing‑placeholder');

    // 1️⃣  Create the SVG and store its internal id (used later for updates)
    const svgMarkup = await makePlaceholderSVG(placeholder, {
      fontColor: '#777',
      fontSize: 16,
      typingSpeed: 100   // wpm – feel free to tweak
    });
    span.innerHTML = svgMarkup;               // inject the SVG
    // Grab the generated id from the markup (it’s something like “typing‑svg‑123”)
    const generatedId = span.querySelector('svg').id;
    span.dataset.svgId = generatedId;

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // 4️⃣  Wire focus / blur events
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    input.addEventListener('focus', async () => {
      // optional: hide the native placeholder attribute
      input.setAttribute('placeholder', '');

      // 2️⃣  Set a short delay before the animation starts
      await setTypingAnimation({delayBeforeStart: 300, typingSpeed: 120});

      // 3️⃣  (Optional) If you want the text to disappear on blur, configure deletion:
      // await customizeDeletionAnimation({deletionSpeed: 150, pauseBeforeRetyping: 400});
    });

    input.addEventListener('blur', async () => {
      // If you want the typed text to stay, do nothing.
      // If you want it to erase and go back to the static placeholder:
      // await customizeDeletionAnimation({deletionSpeed: 150, pauseBeforeRetyping: 400});
      // await setTypingAnimation({delayBeforeStart: 0, typingSpeed: 120}); // re‑type
    });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What the script does

| Line | Explanation |
|------|-------------|
| `makePlaceholderSVG` | Calls the **`createTypingSVG`** API, returns the raw `<svg>` markup. |
| `span.innerHTML = svgMarkup` | Inserts the SVG into the placeholder `<span>`. |
| `setTypingAnimation` | Adjusts the *delay* and *speed* for the next typing run (you can call it each time you want a different speed). |
| `customizeDeletionAnimation` | (Optional) Sets how fast the text disappears and how long to wait before typing again. |
| `input.addEventListener('focus', …)` | Triggers the animation when the user clicks into the field. |
| `input.addEventListener('blur', …)` | (Optional) Handles the “erase‑and‑re‑type” cycle when the field loses focus. |

---

## 3️⃣  Fine‑tuning the animation

| Setting | Typical values | When to use |
|---------|----------------|-------------|
| **`typingSpeed`** (wpm) | 60 – 150 | Faster for short placeholders, slower for longer sentences. |
| **`delayBeforeStart`** (ms) | 200 – 800 | Gives the user a moment to notice the field before the typing begins. |
| **`deletionSpeed`** (wpm) | 80 – 200 | Faster deletion feels snappier; slower gives a “backspace” vibe. |
| **`pauseBeforeRetyping`** (ms) | 300 – 800 | Small pause makes the erase‑then‑type loop feel natural. |
| **`fontColor`** | `#777` (placeholder gray) or any brand colour | Keep it visually distinct from user‑typed text. |
| **`fontSize`** | 14 – 18 (px) | Match the input’s font size for seamless alignment. |

You can change any of these on the fly:

```js
await setTypingAnimation({delayBeforeStart: 500, typingSpeed: 90});
await customizeDeletionAnimation({deletionSpeed: 120, pauseBeforeRetyping: 600});
```

---

## 4️⃣  Updating the placeholder later (e.g., after validation)

If you need to change the text or style after the SVG has already been created, use **`updateTypingSVG`**:

```js
await updateTypingSVG({
  svgId: span.dataset.svgId,
  newText: 'Looks good! Keep typing…',
  newFontColor: '#2a9d8f',
  newFontSize: 16
});
```

